1
00:02:23,868 --> 00:02:26,084
This is a report from the
state Health Department...

2
00:02:26,114 --> 00:02:28,873
and it says some of them bats is rabid.

3
00:02:29,130 --> 00:02:32,100
- Well?
- And that ain't all.

4
00:02:32,522 --> 00:02:36,080
And now there's a rumor going
around that it was the Bat himself...

5
00:02:36,261 --> 00:02:39,849
the killer I mean, that released the
rabid bats in this neighborhood.

6
00:02:39,879 --> 00:02:42,276
Oh, that's ridiculous.

7
00:02:42,775 --> 00:02:47,899
Well, the housekeeper, the cook, the
butler and the upstairs maid don't think so.

8
00:02:47,929 --> 00:02:49,995
Well, I can't help what they think.

9
00:02:50,402 --> 00:02:54,457
If hysterical nonsense like that
can scare them out of their good jobs...

10
00:02:54,638 --> 00:02:56,748
it's their loss not mine.

11
00:02:56,778 --> 00:02:59,266
Come on Lizzy, I've got to get to the bank.

12
00:03:04,859 --> 00:03:07,299
Drive directly to Zenith Bank Warner.

13
00:03:07,329 --> 00:03:10,014
I'm afraid we'll have
to hurry, it's near closing time.

14
00:03:10,044 --> 00:03:11,718
I'll get you there Miss Van Gorder.

15
00:03:24,457 --> 00:03:25,724
Thanks again.

16
00:03:26,809 --> 00:03:29,275
- Miss Van Gorder!
- How are you doing Mr. Bailey?

17
00:03:29,305 --> 00:03:31,367
- How are you?
- I'm very well, thank you.

18
00:03:31,598 --> 00:03:33,027
You remember Lizzy Allen?

19
00:03:33,057 --> 00:03:35,164
- Of course, hello Miss Allen.
- How do you do?

20
00:03:35,494 --> 00:03:37,392
So you're spending the
summer with us again?

21
00:03:37,416 --> 00:03:39,047
Yes, yes, I've
leased the Oaks.,

22
00:03:39,541 --> 00:03:41,571
The home of your bank
president John Fleming.

23
00:03:41,601 --> 00:03:43,851
I heard you had, I was surprised.

24
00:03:43,881 --> 00:03:45,782
Why? Is there something the matter with it?

25
00:03:45,812 --> 00:03:49,109
No, I was surprised because
Mr. Fleming said he would never rent it.

26
00:03:49,289 --> 00:03:50,042
Oh?

27
00:03:50,514 --> 00:03:54,914
Well I rented it from his nephew Mark
Fleming who has the real estate office here.

28
00:03:55,078 --> 00:03:57,856
He said his uncle would
be gone the entire summer.

29
00:03:57,991 --> 00:03:58,879
That's right.

30
00:03:59,256 --> 00:04:02,652
Mr. Fleming is in the north woods
now with his physician Dr. Wells.

31
00:04:03,443 --> 00:04:05,633
Oh, pard me, Dale.

32
00:04:05,942 --> 00:04:08,383
I want you to meet my wife.
We were married at Christmas time.

33
00:04:08,413 --> 00:04:10,506
- That must've been nice.
- Believe me, it was.

34
00:04:10,536 --> 00:04:13,970
Oh, here she is, my wife,
Miss Van Gorder, Miss Allen.

35
00:04:14,115 --> 00:04:16,710
- How do you do Miss Bailey?
- How do you do?

36
00:04:16,740 --> 00:04:19,045
- Cornelia Van Gorder.
- Yes.

37
00:04:19,075 --> 00:04:22,469
Oh, well I've read every murder
mystery you've ever written.

38
00:04:22,499 --> 00:04:25,991
I just adored that weird one,
the private morgue of Dr. X.

39
00:04:26,445 --> 00:04:30,782
- Even though it gave me the shivers.
- Only the shivers? Scared hell out of me.

40
00:04:32,095 --> 00:04:36,418
Well, I, I, I really means that Miss
Corny killed them off in that one.

41
00:04:36,770 --> 00:04:40,359
When you refer to my books,
please don't call me Miss Corny.

42
00:04:40,812 --> 00:04:43,157
Pard me, Mr. Bailey,
Mr. Hynes is here to see you.

43
00:04:43,187 --> 00:04:45,511
Oh yes, excuse me please.

44
00:04:46,248 --> 00:04:48,977
- Don't be strangers now.
- No, no we won't.

45
00:04:49,007 --> 00:04:51,962
Oh, so you're a bride?

46
00:04:51,992 --> 00:04:55,248
- No, not quite.
- Not since Christmas.

47
00:04:55,278 --> 00:04:57,343
You know, I'm sure I've seen you.

48
00:04:57,373 --> 00:05:00,418
Well I, I used to be my
husband's secretary here in the bank.

49
00:05:00,448 --> 00:05:02,951
Of course, I remember.

50
00:05:04,278 --> 00:05:07,429
May I welcome our most
distinguished visitor back to Zenith?
